1
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:24,280
*dissonant violin chords
synced to a metronome*

2
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:49,280
Come closer,
elbows on the table.

3
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:10,680
Your colleagues at the front
think you're a malingerer.

4
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:16,520
You are a recipient
of the Iron Cross First Class.

5
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:19,000
A capable soldier.

6
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:22,800
A man like that wouldn't fake it.

7
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:27,160
Yet hypnosis works primarily
through the eyes.

8
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:33,160
In short, you cannot
hypnotize a blind man.

9
00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:36,040
I cannot help you.

10
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:48,560
(Soldier) Staff Surgeon, sir.

11
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:51,400
Please.

12
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:54,080
I want to see again.

13
00:01:57,400 --> 00:01:58,400
(whispering) Please.

14
00:01:58,480 --> 00:02:01,040
*dramatic drumbeats*

15
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:03,720
Yes.

16
00:02:09,479 --> 00:02:10,800
That would be a miracle.

17
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,840
You're hoping for a miracle?

18
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:19,000
Miracles don't happen anymore.
In our...

19
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:21,280
in our modern world.

20
00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:25,080
Not for ordinary men,

21
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:29,960
but a man
of extraordinary willpower...

22
00:02:30,040 --> 00:02:31,120
*Soldier breathes nervously.*

23
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:33,520
For him, there are no limits.

24
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:35,680
He throws off the shackles.

25
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:38,920
He tears down
the walls of the ordinary.

26
00:02:40,040 --> 00:02:41,200
Examine yourself.

27
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:43,920
Do you believe you have that will?

28
00:02:44,880 --> 00:02:46,760
*suspenseful music*

29
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:51,480
Then let us try.

30
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:01,120
*tones become brighter*

31
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:02,800
Open your eyes.

32
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:04,920
Try it.
*Doctor blows.*

33
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:08,280
Did you see the spark?

34
00:03:12,640 --> 00:03:13,920
I don't know.

35
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:15,360
*music quickens*

36
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:18,680
Maybe a glimmer.

37
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:21,080
That's not enough.
That won't do.

38
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:26,040
In every man lies a god.

39
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:28,200
That is the will.

40
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:30,480
That is the energy.

41
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:34,320
Focus all that power inside you.

42
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:38,320
You feel this power.

43
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:43,640
You know this power
can accomplish superhuman feats.

44
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:44,800
Yes.

45
00:03:45,920 --> 00:03:47,280
I know that.

46
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:50,120
The flame.

47
00:03:52,640 --> 00:03:53,880
Do you see the flame?

48
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:54,960
I want to!

49
00:03:55,480 --> 00:03:56,480
But...

50
00:03:56,640 --> 00:03:58,960
*music intensifies dramatically*

51
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:00,800
*Soldier breathes heavily.*
You must see.

52
00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:03,400
Anything is possible for you.

53
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:04,680
More.

54
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:06,760
*Soldier groans with effort.*
More.

55
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:09,840
More!
*music stops abruptly*

56
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:14,280
*eerie music*

57
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:41,160
*rhythmic music*

58
00:04:58,120 --> 00:05:00,720
*"Mir ist so nach dir"
by Mischa Spoliansky*

59
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:03,120
*lively music*

60
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:25,480
# I feel so much for you #

61
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:28,480
# I felt so much for you yesterday #

62
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:31,560
# And I always will #

63
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:35,240
# I'd love nothing more
than to be alone with you #

64
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:37,720
# And even if you laugh at it #

65
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:40,720
# And whatever you do against it #

66
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:46,120
# Today deep down inside me
I yearn for you #

67
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:49,920
# I don't know:
What's going on with you? #

68
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:52,640
# Going on with me?
Going on with me? #

69
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:55,520
# I don't know,
what's the matter with me? #

70
00:05:55,600 --> 00:06:00,720
# And how about you,
me, me, me, me? #

71
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:04,480
When reporting the news, you have to
let the words float more freely.

72
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:06,960
Without bias, but with depth.

73
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:09,560
And with an awareness
of the drama of the moment.

74
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:12,200
That's your field.
I do the light entertainment.

75
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:14,960
Nonsense, you have the voice,
you're just holding back.

76
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:17,840
Besides, I have to prep the radio play
in Studio 2.

77
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:19,120
I can take care of that.

78
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:22,040
Gentlemen: our colleague Jacoby.

79
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:23,120
Morning...
- Morning.

80
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:24,840
The new voice of Germany.

81
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:29,360
Alright, focus, study the script.

82
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:35,280
Distance to the microphone.

83
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:37,240
Too far.

84
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:39,120
*music fades*

85
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:45,680
Attention, attention,
this is Funkstunde News.

86
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:47,040
It is Monday,

87
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:52,000
January 30th, 1933,
11:30 AM, dear listeners.

88
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:55,080
We turn our attention
to the events

89
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:58,080
unfolding at this hour
in the government quarter.

90
00:06:58,160 --> 00:06:59,960
Will Reich President Hindenburg

91
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:01,880
appoint the leader
of the National Socialist

92
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:04,080
German Workers' Party,
Adolf Hitler,

93
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:05,800
as the new Reich Chancellor?

94
00:07:05,960 --> 00:07:08,920
Excuse me, can I get through?
- Negotiations have been going on since morning.

95
00:07:09,080 --> 00:07:10,600
Any news from the front?

96
00:07:10,760 --> 00:07:12,680
Word on the street is

97
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:14,640
that Hitler is making
hard demands.

98
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:16,880
Such as?
- First and foremost, new elections.

99
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:18,480
And as soon as possible.

100
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:21,280
He won't be a chancellor
by Hindenburg's grace.

101
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,000
He wants the people to elect him.
- Yes.

102
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:32,520
*men whispering*

103
00:07:56,920 --> 00:07:58,240
*door slams shut*

104
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:15,600
Dr. Forster?

105
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:30,600
Hello?

106
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:32,360
*suspenseful music*

107
00:08:33,159 --> 00:08:34,320
Is someone there?

108
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:57,240
Hello?

109
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:03,320
*man breathes nervously*

110
00:09:09,520 --> 00:09:10,560
*ominous tones*

111
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:24,240
*phone rings*

112
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:52,880
*she sighs*

113
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:54,880
Inspection A, Ritter speaking.

114
00:09:55,040 --> 00:09:56,120
Who's there?

115
00:09:59,080 --> 00:10:00,200
Hello.

116
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:19,320
What's going on?

117
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:23,520
(quietly) Dr. Forster wasn't there,
and the file wasn't either.

118
00:10:44,160 --> 00:10:45,400
Police Precinct 5.

119
00:10:45,480 --> 00:10:46,600
Yes, I...

120
00:10:47,960 --> 00:10:49,960
I'd like to make
an anonymous report.

121
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:51,600
What exactly is this regarding?

122
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:54,720
A murder.

123
00:10:59,080 --> 00:11:00,760
*suspenseful music*

124
00:11:02,760 --> 00:11:04,200
*quiet murmuring*

125
00:11:09,520 --> 00:11:10,560
What is he doing here?

126
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:14,280
Uh, the doctor, Forster...
- He wasn't there.

127
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:16,800
And the file?

128
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:19,200
We searched the whole clinic.
- We'll find him.

129
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:20,840
And the file.

130
00:11:21,280 --> 00:11:24,240
The Führer is counting
on you personally, Blank.

131
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:29,480
*music fades out*

132
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:32,440
Take this down: Breaking news.

133
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:35,200
Berlin. The Reich President...

134
00:11:35,360 --> 00:11:38,120
Field Marshal Hindenburg
has just appointed...

135
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:41,840
Adolf Hitler as Reich Chancellor
of Germany.

136
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:44,360
The new Reich Chancellor
has stipulated

137
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:46,280
that he will govern with
the majority support

138
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:48,440
of the German people.

139
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:52,600
Therefore, new elections have been
scheduled for March 5th.

140
00:11:52,680 --> 00:11:54,880
He really won the old man over.

141
00:11:55,920 --> 00:11:57,360
He didn't do it alone.

142
00:11:58,160 --> 00:11:59,920
That was the work of many.

143
00:12:02,280 --> 00:12:03,640
Back to work, Katelbach.

144
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:06,520
Yeah, already on it.
- See you at the Press Ball.

145
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:08,840
Not this time.
Personal obligations.

146
00:12:08,920 --> 00:12:11,880
But I'll be there for the after-party
at Café Mutzbauer.

147
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:19,600
(scattered shouts) Heil!

148
00:12:22,960 --> 00:12:25,040
*threatening music*

149
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:46,120
Here, 2:30, at Opernplatz.

150
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:49,040
*gloomy music*

151
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:36,520
Morning.
Morning.

152
00:13:40,920 --> 00:13:41,960
Morning, colleagues.

153
00:13:42,080 --> 00:13:43,080
Morning.

154
00:13:43,200 --> 00:13:44,200
Morning.

155
00:13:44,360 --> 00:13:45,480
Morning.

156
00:13:48,680 --> 00:13:51,040
Which one of you took
the anonymous call?

157
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:52,240
I did, Mrs...

158
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:54,400
Detective.

159
00:14:00,040 --> 00:14:02,240
Has anyone disturbed anything here?

160
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:04,280
No, we waited for you.

161
00:14:04,440 --> 00:14:06,200
Good. Thank you.

162
00:14:09,320 --> 00:14:11,560
What exactly
did the caller see?

163
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:14,320
That the doctor rushed away.

164
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:16,160
Down the stairs, that is.
I see.

165
00:14:16,320 --> 00:14:17,320
Where's the body?

166
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:19,600
In the next room.

167
00:14:20,520 --> 00:14:21,520
Let's get to work.

168
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:26,080
*she coughs*

169
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:27,840
*foreboding music*

170
00:14:36,240 --> 00:14:39,720
*street noise*

171
00:15:03,920 --> 00:15:05,600
*sinister sound*

172
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:10,560
Are you looking for me?

173
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:15,760
Then I bid you good day.

174
00:15:27,120 --> 00:15:28,320
Officer!

175
00:15:28,400 --> 00:15:29,400
Officer!

176
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:32,400
I'm being followed.
- Is that so?

177
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:33,840
That SA man.

178
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:35,640
He's been following me.

179
00:15:35,720 --> 00:15:37,920
Ever since I
got off the subway.

180
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:39,480
That guy? He's just looking.

181
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:41,920
I'm a lawyer.

182
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:44,520
You walk over to him
and take down his details.

183
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:46,280
Or I will take action against you!

184
00:15:58,200 --> 00:16:00,480
*music turns restless*

185
00:16:10,400 --> 00:16:12,280
(Woman) That would be the first proposal?

186
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:14,120
No, I want to know specifically

187
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:16,760
who I'm dealing with.

188
00:16:17,240 --> 00:16:18,680
I don't need to know every detail.

189
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:22,240
We're not putting this man's first name
on page one, not a chance.

190
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:23,720
That's all we need.

191
00:16:23,800 --> 00:16:25,320
(Woman) That's what I thought.

192
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:28,400
Alright, something like that.

193
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,400
Short and painful.

194
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:32,880
Excuse me, Mr. Editor-in-Chief.
- What is it?

195
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:35,760
The mugshot needs to go in.
The police insist on it.

196
00:16:35,920 --> 00:16:38,040
Squeeze it onto the police page

197
00:16:38,120 --> 00:16:41,400
and don't interrupt us
with such trifles, Potocznik.

198
00:16:41,560 --> 00:16:43,360
Especially not on a day like this.

199
00:16:43,440 --> 00:16:44,800
Otherwise, I also have

200
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:48,000
an advance review of
'The Testament of Dr. Mabuse'.

201
00:16:48,160 --> 00:16:50,800
Masterpiece, Fritz Lang,
Rudolf Klein-Rogge,

202
00:16:50,960 --> 00:16:52,760
front-page material, absolutely.

203
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:55,360
Tempo editorial desk?

204
00:16:55,440 --> 00:16:58,560
Hello, please connect me
with the editor-in-chief, Mr. Heymann.

205
00:16:58,640 --> 00:17:00,840
Our editor-in-chief
is very busy.

206
00:17:00,920 --> 00:17:04,040
Would you please...
- It is of the utmost urgency.

207
00:17:04,119 --> 00:17:06,560
Look,
I can't disturb him right now...

208
00:17:06,640 --> 00:17:10,040
I have vital information
concerning the new government.

209
00:17:10,119 --> 00:17:11,240
*he breathes shakily*

210
00:17:11,839 --> 00:17:13,720
Excuse me,
Mr. Editor-in-Chief?

211
00:17:13,800 --> 00:17:14,839
Potocznik!

212
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:17,240
I have someone on the line

213
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:18,960
who claims that...

214
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:22,280
I'll roast you on a spit
if you're pulling my leg.

215
00:17:22,440 --> 00:17:24,800
We have mutual friends
from our university days.

216
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:27,720
The Dahlem circle.
- What was your name again?

217
00:17:28,160 --> 00:17:31,480
Forster, Edmund.
Medicine. You were journalism.

218
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:33,560
New faculty.

219
00:17:33,720 --> 00:17:34,840
And you were saying?

220
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:38,840
I possess information
of extraordinary gravity.

221
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:42,400
Sensitive regarding, against,
about, for what or whom?

222
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:45,040
The new Reich Chancellor.

223
00:17:46,880 --> 00:17:47,880
Go on.

224
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:50,800
I must meet you
in a safe place.

225
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:55,240
Come here. To the newsroom.

226
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:57,280
Out of the question. Public.

227
00:17:58,080 --> 00:18:01,320
Lots of people...
Anonymity, you understand?

228
00:18:02,400 --> 00:18:04,440
Then come to the Press Ball.

229
00:18:04,520 --> 00:18:05,920
You won't find a more anonymous place.

230
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:07,400
Understood.

231
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:08,960
Thank you.

232
00:18:11,800 --> 00:18:13,240
*curious music*

233
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:18,840
*phone rings*

234
00:18:26,720 --> 00:18:28,880
Institute for Suggestive Therapy.

235
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:30,240
Forster speaking.

236
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:32,840
Professor.

237
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:34,480
I need your help.

238
00:18:36,760 --> 00:18:38,080
*door slams shut*

239
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:27,360
*ominous sounds*

240
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:30,080
*mysterious music*

241
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:46,960
Ah, Reinhold.

242
00:19:48,360 --> 00:19:50,120
Well? How was the dentist?

243
00:19:50,280 --> 00:19:51,520
No big deal.

244
00:19:52,880 --> 00:19:54,360
A rotten molar.

245
00:19:55,320 --> 00:19:57,520
With a sweet tooth like mine,
no surprise.

246
00:19:59,200 --> 00:20:01,920
Did I miss anything today?
The change of government.

247
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:03,840
Hardly possible to miss
around town.

248
00:20:03,920 --> 00:20:04,920
And a murder.

249
00:20:05,600 --> 00:20:07,480
There's a prime suspect too.

250
00:20:07,560 --> 00:20:08,560
I see.

251
00:20:09,040 --> 00:20:10,880
Dr. Forster, Edmund.

252
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:12,640
An anonymous caller apparently saw

253
00:20:12,800 --> 00:20:14,760
him leave the crime scene
in a hurry.

254
00:20:15,320 --> 00:20:16,320
Is that so?

255
00:20:18,320 --> 00:20:20,040
It's already gone out to the press.

256
00:20:20,120 --> 00:20:21,880
Can you make copies of this
for tomorrow?

257
00:20:21,960 --> 00:20:23,200
Yes, no problem.

258
00:20:32,960 --> 00:20:35,040
*marching footsteps*

259
00:20:56,160 --> 00:20:58,320
Institute for Suggestive Therapy?

260
00:20:58,400 --> 00:21:00,760
It's me.
Strelow wasn't alone.

261
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:03,080
He was accompanied
by his SA squad.

262
00:21:03,160 --> 00:21:05,720
You didn't hand over the package?
No.

263
00:21:06,400 --> 00:21:07,760
It was impossible.

264
00:21:07,920 --> 00:21:09,360
I understand.

265
00:21:09,440 --> 00:21:11,000
I need to meet you.

266
00:21:11,080 --> 00:21:13,920
Can you slip into the Press Ball
unnoticed?

267
00:21:14,880 --> 00:21:16,360
I'll try.

268
00:21:16,440 --> 00:21:17,480
Good.

269
00:21:18,600 --> 00:21:20,160
Thank you, Gereon.

270
00:21:21,680 --> 00:21:24,000
*sinister music*

271
00:21:43,600 --> 00:21:44,840
Well...
*he starts up*

272
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:47,800
*indistinct voice on radio*

273
00:21:47,960 --> 00:21:49,960
...from every walk of life,

274
00:21:50,040 --> 00:21:52,000
marching past here,

275
00:21:52,160 --> 00:21:55,600
workers of brain and brawn,

276
00:21:55,760 --> 00:21:57,880
all class distinctions
have been erased.

277
00:21:57,960 --> 00:22:02,720
It is a wind like there perhaps
once was in 1813.

278
00:22:02,800 --> 00:22:04,800
When they said, the King called...

279
00:22:04,880 --> 00:22:06,960
(Viennese accent)
This is unbearable.

280
00:22:07,520 --> 00:22:10,400
New elections
in five weeks.

281
00:22:10,560 --> 00:22:12,520
Which hardly makes it any better.

282
00:22:16,160 --> 00:22:18,320
One more sip of lemon balm spirit

283
00:22:18,400 --> 00:22:20,840
and by tomorrow morning
you'll be your old self again.

284
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:25,000
I mean your new self, uh...
good as new, I wanted to say.

285
00:22:27,400 --> 00:22:29,440
Hold on, are you trying to kill me?

286
00:22:29,520 --> 00:22:32,160
Soothingly caresses
the lining of your stomach.

287
00:22:39,800 --> 00:22:41,800
Your hangover will be history faster

288
00:22:41,880 --> 00:22:44,320
than this farce put on
by my unfortunate countryman.

289
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:46,880
I have to leave soon, unfortunately.

290
00:22:47,040 --> 00:22:50,160
You just stay put
and let it work.

291
00:22:52,960 --> 00:22:55,400
*soft piano music*

292
00:22:59,760 --> 00:23:00,920
People heard

293
00:23:01,080 --> 00:23:03,840
that Hitler had been appointed
Reich Chancellor,

294
00:23:03,920 --> 00:23:05,760
that the Hitler-Hindenburg
agreement...

295
00:23:14,160 --> 00:23:15,480
*keys rustling*

296
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:16,720
Finally.

297
00:23:18,320 --> 00:23:19,360
I'm sorry.

298
00:23:21,760 --> 00:23:23,800
If you only knew
what's going on out there.

299
00:23:23,880 --> 00:23:25,720
Half the city is on the move.

300
00:23:25,800 --> 00:23:27,040
Yes, I know.

301
00:23:27,880 --> 00:23:29,400
But I'm here now.

302
00:23:29,560 --> 00:23:31,720
How do I look?
*he huffs*

303
00:23:31,800 --> 00:23:32,840
Dangerous.

304
00:23:37,680 --> 00:23:40,480
And Jacoby still had tickets
for the Press Ball?

305
00:23:41,360 --> 00:23:42,360
Apparently.

306
00:23:46,640 --> 00:23:48,040
They're waiting for us.

307
00:23:55,840 --> 00:23:57,360
We really have to hurry.

308
00:23:57,520 --> 00:23:58,960
Yeah?
Yeah.

309
00:23:59,520 --> 00:24:01,200
Then let's hurry up.

310
00:24:05,480 --> 00:24:07,240
Come on, get dressed up.

311
00:24:09,240 --> 00:24:12,240
*music fades*
*engine spluttering*

312
00:24:15,760 --> 00:24:17,120
You have lipstick right there.

313
00:24:19,080 --> 00:24:20,760
I hope it's mine.

314
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:25,680
Who knows where you've been
gadding about all day.

315
00:24:35,320 --> 00:24:36,480
Did you hear?

316
00:24:37,040 --> 00:24:38,480
Hitler is Chancellor.

317
00:24:39,640 --> 00:24:40,640
Yes.

318
00:24:50,560 --> 00:24:53,280
*suspenseful pulsing music*

319
00:25:10,520 --> 00:25:12,560
*quiet chatter*

320
00:25:15,840 --> 00:25:17,840
*voices grow louder*

321
00:25:35,240 --> 00:25:36,240
Well?

322
00:25:37,120 --> 00:25:38,520
Do you have the medical report?

323
00:25:44,560 --> 00:25:45,960
It didn't work out.

324
00:25:46,040 --> 00:25:47,160
What?

325
00:25:48,680 --> 00:25:49,800
Why?

326
00:25:49,880 --> 00:25:53,560
The doctor, Dr. Forster, has...

327
00:25:55,680 --> 00:25:56,680
disappeared.

328
00:26:03,800 --> 00:26:05,240
Quite a crowd here.

329
00:26:07,360 --> 00:26:09,600
*opulent orchestral music*

330
00:26:22,760 --> 00:26:24,840
Pretty close.
I've got this.

331
00:26:25,400 --> 00:26:27,080
Pardon us, please.
It's my fault.

332
00:26:27,160 --> 00:26:28,760
(Gräf) We're late too.

333
00:26:30,040 --> 00:26:31,080
Together, please.

334
00:26:31,160 --> 00:26:32,920
Let's mingle with the crowd.

335
00:26:33,080 --> 00:26:35,120
*music becomes livelier*

336
00:26:48,800 --> 00:26:50,840
*indistinct dialogue*

337
00:26:51,440 --> 00:26:53,400
How's it going?
- Half of Tempo is here.

338
00:27:10,520 --> 00:27:13,160
Where did you find her?
In the back of the clinic.

339
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:15,400
In bed,
wearing only a nightgown.

340
00:27:16,120 --> 00:27:17,720
The doctor was seen

341
00:27:17,880 --> 00:27:19,920
leaving the building in a rush.

342
00:27:21,560 --> 00:27:23,280
Thank goodness, there you are.

343
00:27:29,760 --> 00:27:30,800
That's him.

344
00:27:31,480 --> 00:27:33,480
You won't believe this.
What?

345
00:27:34,280 --> 00:27:35,480
That's him.

346
00:27:35,560 --> 00:27:37,400
Who?
The doctor from the building today.

347
00:27:38,400 --> 00:27:39,600
Are you sure?

348
00:27:41,080 --> 00:27:42,840
His name is Dr. Forster.

349
00:27:43,880 --> 00:27:46,840
Do you have your badge on you?
I always have it on me.

350
00:27:47,000 --> 00:27:48,000
I don't.

351
00:27:48,080 --> 00:27:49,320
You approach him, alright?
Alright.

352
00:27:50,440 --> 00:27:52,640
You go up the left, I'll take the right.
Good.

353
00:27:54,080 --> 00:27:55,160
I'll get Gräf.

354
00:27:56,080 --> 00:27:57,880
Give me a head start.
Will do.

355
00:28:07,120 --> 00:28:08,640
What?
- Take a look.

356
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:13,520
*murmuring*

357
00:28:14,480 --> 00:28:16,440
I need your help.
Look up there.

358
00:28:17,560 --> 00:28:19,040
(Gräf) Dr. Forster?

359
00:28:20,240 --> 00:28:21,240
Come with me.

360
00:28:23,600 --> 00:28:25,480
This gentleman's life is in danger.

361
00:28:25,640 --> 00:28:27,800
You are being accused of a crime.

362
00:28:27,960 --> 00:28:29,680
They want to silence me.

363
00:28:32,280 --> 00:28:33,800
We have to leave right now.

364
00:28:52,080 --> 00:28:55,560
You've got to be kidding.
He was right here a second ago.

365
00:28:55,640 --> 00:28:57,160
I'll check over there.
Yeah.

366
00:28:57,880 --> 00:29:00,000
*music turns more dynamic*

367
00:29:06,640 --> 00:29:09,280
*music builds dramatically*

368
00:29:10,440 --> 00:29:11,760
*music ends*

369
00:29:11,840 --> 00:29:13,200
*she gasps*

370
00:29:13,280 --> 00:29:15,080
*jazzy drum beats*

371
00:29:17,800 --> 00:29:18,800
Gereon?

372
00:29:23,600 --> 00:29:25,960
*music swells dramatically*

373
00:29:32,520 --> 00:29:34,000
*music ends*

374
00:29:43,800 --> 00:29:46,560
*dynamic lute music*

375
00:30:08,480 --> 00:30:11,440
It's quarter past nine,
dinner was set for eight.

376
00:30:11,520 --> 00:30:12,600
He's not here yet.

377
00:30:27,880 --> 00:30:29,280
*he sneezes loudly*

378
00:30:33,040 --> 00:30:35,160
*music fades, applause*

379
00:30:35,320 --> 00:30:37,120
(Spectator) Bravo, Nyssen!

380
00:30:37,200 --> 00:30:40,040
(Helga) Alfred.
Thank you from the bottom of our hearts.

381
00:30:40,120 --> 00:30:41,680
I'm not playing another piece, though.

382
00:30:43,120 --> 00:30:44,720
He said he'd come at eight.

383
00:30:45,360 --> 00:30:47,920
Come now, take it easy,
my dear Nyssen.

384
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:50,400
New responsibilities,
new obligations.

385
00:30:50,480 --> 00:30:53,040
You mean
one can just forget the old ones?

386
00:30:53,200 --> 00:30:54,240
(Helga) He will come.

387
00:30:54,400 --> 00:30:57,400
I have always found Mr. Hitler
to be very reliable.

388
00:30:57,480 --> 00:30:59,760
As long as he
still needed our money, yes.

389
00:30:59,840 --> 00:31:01,320
Let's just get started.

390
00:31:01,480 --> 00:31:04,120
As we know, the Führer
doesn't care much for food.

391
00:31:04,680 --> 00:31:07,400
Nor for this.
*subdued laughter*

392
00:31:07,480 --> 00:31:09,640
My dear Göring,
this evening isn't about

393
00:31:09,720 --> 00:31:12,040
stuffing our faces.

394
00:31:12,120 --> 00:31:15,200
It is about
Mr. Hitler explaining to his backers,

395
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:18,000
or rather his benefactors,

396
00:31:18,160 --> 00:31:22,160
how he will now,
since the hour has arrived,

397
00:31:22,240 --> 00:31:24,360
lead Germany to where
we all envision it.

398
00:31:25,040 --> 00:31:26,480
I personally handed him
a ten-point plan,

399
00:31:27,560 --> 00:31:30,760
and now I'd like to know

400
00:31:30,920 --> 00:31:32,760
in what stages

401
00:31:32,840 --> 00:31:35,640
he will put it into effect.

402
00:31:36,320 --> 00:31:38,240
Now that he is finally in the office

403
00:31:39,280 --> 00:31:41,120
we put him in.

404
00:31:42,560 --> 00:31:44,840
Excuse me for a moment.
- Of course.

405
00:31:46,200 --> 00:31:48,960
Alfred, that wasn't very diplomatic
just now.

406
00:31:49,040 --> 00:31:51,680
It's the only language
these parvenus understand.

407
00:31:52,760 --> 00:31:54,960
Gentlemen,
you can call me

408
00:31:55,120 --> 00:31:57,200
if the Herr Chancellor
decides to show up after all.

409
00:31:57,960 --> 00:32:00,000
We should begin
before everything is overcooked

410
00:32:00,160 --> 00:32:01,960
and loses all its flavor.

411
00:32:02,040 --> 00:32:03,760
Please, we're serving.

412
00:32:04,640 --> 00:32:08,320
If I may invite the guests to table,
dinner is served.

413
00:32:16,680 --> 00:32:17,920
Thank you.
- Yes.

414
00:32:18,640 --> 00:32:20,560
Rath was standing up on the gallery.

415
00:32:20,720 --> 00:32:23,520
With Dr. Forster.
And someone else.

416
00:32:23,680 --> 00:32:26,160
Then suddenly he vanished.
And?

417
00:32:26,720 --> 00:32:29,280
Looked everywhere.
He must have arrested him.

418
00:32:29,840 --> 00:32:30,960
The doctor?

419
00:32:32,600 --> 00:32:34,760
Then he probably took him
to the Burg.

420
00:32:34,840 --> 00:32:36,120
Safe to assume, yes.

421
00:32:37,960 --> 00:32:39,840
No, he's not here.

422
00:32:40,480 --> 00:32:41,480
Any notes?

423
00:32:42,520 --> 00:32:44,440
Yes, let's take a look.

424
00:32:45,440 --> 00:32:46,440
Hold on.

425
00:32:53,520 --> 00:32:54,520
Nothing!

426
00:32:55,440 --> 00:32:58,280
Nothing!
I'm sorry, Miss Ritter.

427
00:32:59,400 --> 00:33:00,640
Yes, goodbye!

428
00:33:03,880 --> 00:33:06,840
(Helga) Well then,
actually this evening we wanted

429
00:33:07,000 --> 00:33:10,440
to hear from Mr. Hitler
how Germany's future

430
00:33:10,600 --> 00:33:12,000
will become a new reality.

431
00:33:12,600 --> 00:33:14,120
Now, of all people,

432
00:33:14,280 --> 00:33:17,000
the key visionaries
are not present.

433
00:33:18,440 --> 00:33:21,920
Perhaps you would like to speak,
honorable Reichstag President?

434
00:33:22,600 --> 00:33:26,040
Dear Hermann Göring,
would you care to say a few words

435
00:33:26,200 --> 00:33:28,440
befitting this momentous hour?

436
00:33:29,880 --> 00:33:31,600
What is there to say?

437
00:33:31,760 --> 00:33:33,960
Things will not remain
as they were.

438
00:33:34,040 --> 00:33:35,040
*murmurs of agreement*

439
00:33:35,120 --> 00:33:37,840
We must clean out the pigsty

440
00:33:37,920 --> 00:33:40,920
bequeathed to us by the system,
and quickly.

441
00:33:41,000 --> 00:33:43,800
We are not here
to administer justice.

442
00:33:43,880 --> 00:33:46,520
Our only task is to destroy
and eradicate.

443
00:33:46,600 --> 00:33:49,000
(Dr. Völcker)
I spent two years in Moscow.

444
00:33:49,080 --> 00:33:53,080
For two years, I was prepared
for this exact day.

445
00:33:54,160 --> 00:33:56,560
The line of General Secretary Stalin

446
00:33:56,640 --> 00:33:59,120
and Chairman Thälmann
is unmistakable.

447
00:34:00,080 --> 00:34:02,400
Escalation in this situation

448
00:34:02,480 --> 00:34:04,120
would be entirely
the wrong approach.

449
00:34:04,200 --> 00:34:05,560
(Man) Comrade Völcker!

450
00:34:05,720 --> 00:34:09,679
The line from the leadership in Moscow
is not decisive here.

451
00:34:10,199 --> 00:34:12,600
They're 2,000 kilometers
away from us.

452
00:34:13,320 --> 00:34:17,880
The fight must be waged here and now
in the streets!

453
00:34:18,040 --> 00:34:19,679
Exactly!

454
00:34:20,880 --> 00:34:23,480
(Heymann)
Colleagues, friends, companions,

455
00:34:23,560 --> 00:34:26,360
I fear this will all last
much longer

456
00:34:26,520 --> 00:34:28,520
than most of us believe.

457
00:34:28,600 --> 00:34:30,600
Yet we are not powerless.

458
00:34:31,239 --> 00:34:33,159
Every one of us can make a choice

459
00:34:33,320 --> 00:34:35,800
and never give an inch

460
00:34:35,880 --> 00:34:38,360
to those who are now grasping
for power.

461
00:34:38,840 --> 00:34:40,639
What we need is a powerful,

462
00:34:40,719 --> 00:34:43,159
vehement sign
from many voices.

463
00:34:43,320 --> 00:34:46,719
An appeal to reason
for the elections in five weeks.

464
00:34:46,880 --> 00:34:48,000
*dark music*

465
00:34:48,080 --> 00:34:50,719
We must mobilize
everyone we can.

466
00:34:50,800 --> 00:34:53,560
In the coming days, we will replace
all police presidents

467
00:34:53,639 --> 00:34:56,679
with men we can rely on.

468
00:34:56,840 --> 00:34:59,600
Our esteemed retired Rear Admiral,
Herr von Levetzow,

469
00:34:59,680 --> 00:35:01,760
will become Police President of Berlin.

470
00:35:03,640 --> 00:35:07,320
(Göring) The political police will be
severed from standard administration

471
00:35:07,480 --> 00:35:10,480
and replaced by
a Secret State Police Office.

472
00:35:11,120 --> 00:35:13,840
Senior Government Councillor Wendt
will assume command.

473
00:35:13,920 --> 00:35:18,320
SA units will be assigned
alongside police officers

474
00:35:18,400 --> 00:35:20,360
to suppress the unrest

475
00:35:20,520 --> 00:35:24,360
expected from the radical left
during the elections.

476
00:35:25,120 --> 00:35:27,440
Police officers who use firearms

477
00:35:27,600 --> 00:35:29,800
in the line of duty

478
00:35:29,880 --> 00:35:32,200
will have my personal backing.

479
00:35:32,680 --> 00:35:35,680
The election in five weeks
must be won.

480
00:35:35,840 --> 00:35:39,600
That red scum cannot be allowed
to spoil our plans, can they?

481
00:35:39,760 --> 00:35:41,640
(Man) Hear, hear!
*applause*

482
00:35:44,320 --> 00:35:45,720
(Göring) Speaking of soup,

483
00:35:45,800 --> 00:35:48,040
we shouldn't let it get cold.

484
00:35:50,960 --> 00:35:52,040
Gereon?

485
00:36:18,920 --> 00:36:20,880
*mournful piano music*

486
00:36:34,800 --> 00:36:36,880
Can I get you anything else?
No, thank you.

487
00:36:54,040 --> 00:36:55,480
*doorbell chimes*

488
00:37:00,160 --> 00:37:01,360
*music fades out*

489
00:37:05,320 --> 00:37:07,880
Excuse me,
I must have made a mistake.

490
00:37:09,240 --> 00:37:10,640
Who are you looking for?

491
00:37:12,960 --> 00:37:17,520
Gereon Rath. We had an appointment
and I'm late.

492
00:37:17,680 --> 00:37:19,080
I need to pick something up.

493
00:37:19,160 --> 00:37:21,000
What do you need to pick up?

494
00:37:22,560 --> 00:37:24,560
Nothing. Excuse me.

495
00:37:27,600 --> 00:37:30,520
*mournful piano music continues*

496
00:37:32,000 --> 00:37:33,000
*

